{%- comment -%}
  YMAL — Recently Viewed RECORDER. Records the product being viewed; renders
  nothing.

  Usage, in layout/theme.liquid just before </body>:

    {%- if template.name == 'product' -%}
      {%- render 'ymal-recently-viewed-recorder', product: product -%}
    {%- endif -%}

  WHY THIS EXISTS

  Recently Viewed has two halves that live in different places. RECORDING has
  to happen on a product page: that is the only place a shopper views one. But
  the web team wanted it DISPLAYED only in the cart drawer, and the cart
  drawer's snippet never records - it only reads.

  The display snippet (ymal-recently-viewed.liquid) records as a side effect of
  rendering a visible row. Using it for recording alone would have put a second
  recommendation row on every product page, directly beside the Featured row,
  competing for the same attention. This snippet is the recording half on its
  own, so where Recently Viewed is SHOWN can change without anyone having to
  think about where it is RECORDED.

  It is also what Inspired By Your Views will build on.

  SAFE ALONGSIDE THE DISPLAY SNIPPET

  If ymal-recently-viewed.liquid is later placed on a product page as well, both
  load ymal-recently-viewed.js. The script guards against running twice, so the
  product is recorded once and no card is appended twice.

  `product` must be passed explicitly: `render` gives a snippet its own scope,
  and without it this would silently record nothing.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if product -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Handle and id only. Title, price and image are fetched fresh wherever the
    list is displayed, so nothing stored in the shopper's browser can go stale.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="application/json" id="ymal-current-product">
    {"handle": {{ product.handle | json }}, "id": {{ product.id | json }}}
  </script>
  <script src="{{ 'ymal-recently-viewed.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
